  "paper_text": {
    "footnote_or_appendix": "At the highest dosage (d100, 10\\%), all benchmark items are contaminated ($n_{\\text{untreated}}=0$), precluding the treated-vs-untreated DiD design. At d050 (5\\%), the most balanced split ($n_{\\text{treated}} \\approx n_{\\text{untreated}}$), MDES is 1.1--2.0\\,pp for MMLU and 2.4--6.6\\,pp for ARC-Challenge (80\\% power, $\\alpha=0.05$). Doubling the treated sample from d025 to d050 yields only marginal MDES improvement on MMLU ($\\sim$0.1\\,pp) and no improvement on ARC, indicating that item-level variance, not sample size, is the binding constraint."
  }
